{%- comment -%}
  Product list: a heading area (any theme blocks: Heading, Text, Buttons...) above products from a
  collection, in one of four layouts (setting "Layout"):
  - Grid: the big product cards in columns (homepage "Featured products" / "New arrivals", M4)
  - Compact rows: small glass rows with a quick add button ("You might love" under the empty cart)
  - Scrolling strip: one row of big cards that scrolls sideways, with arrows
  - Tabs: one tab per "Tab" block (label + collection), e.g. New / Bestsellers / Under $50
  One file, four presets: the theme editor's "Add section" list shows each layout by name.

  "Only when the cart is empty": for the cart page. The section then renders nothing while the cart
  has items, and the cart's script renders it again (data-cart-refresh) when the cart changes, so it
  appears when the last item is removed and disappears when something is added.

  Without products (no collection chosen, or an empty one) it shows placeholder cards in the theme
  editor and its "Add section" preview only; on the store the section shows nothing (a Tab without
  products is left out).
  Tabs: each Tab block draws its own tab button and panel (blocks/_product-tab): a section can't read
  its theme blocks' settings (section.blocks gives them as "@theme" with empty settings).
  Compact rows: 1 per row on phones, 2 per row from 750px (mockup "Main" of the empty bag).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign layout = section.settings.layout | default: 'grid'
  assign product_collection = section.settings.collection
  assign limit = section.settings.products_to_show
  assign columns_desktop = section.settings.columns_desktop
  assign columns_mobile = section.settings.columns_mobile | plus: 0

  assign hidden_by_cart = false
  if section.settings.show_only_empty_cart and cart.item_count > 0
    assign hidden_by_cart = true
  endif

  # Products: placeholders only in the theme editor and in its "Add section" preview
  # (visual_preview_mode); on the store, no products = no section.
  assign editor = false
  if request.design_mode or request.visual_preview_mode
    assign editor = true
  endif
  # Tabs: the section can't read its Tab blocks (theme block settings are only readable in the block's
  # own file), so each Tab decides itself whether it shows; a tab row with no Tab = no section (CSS :has).
  assign show_section = true
  if layout != 'tabs'
    unless product_collection.products_count > 0 or editor
      assign show_section = false
    endunless
  endif

  capture card_sizes
    render 'product-list-sizes'
  endcapture
  assign card_sizes = card_sizes | strip

  # Never animate the first section on the page (hero / LCP must paint immediately)
  assign animation = section.settings.animation
  if section.index == 1
    assign animation = 'none'
  endif
-%}

{%- if hidden_by_cart or show_section == false -%}
  {%- comment -%} Kept so the cart's script knows to render this section again when the cart changes {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if section.settings.show_only_empty_cart -%}
    <div data-cart-refresh hidden></div>
    {%- comment -%}
      The cards come later (the cart's script renders this section again when the bag is empty), so
      the card and cart button scripts must be in this first HTML
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if hidden_by_cart -%}
      {%- assign scripts_product = product_collection.products.first | default: cart.items.first.product -%}
      {% render 'card-scripts', product: scripts_product %}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- else -%}
  <div
    class="product-list product-list--{{ layout }}{% unless editor %} product-list--live{% endunless %} full-width section-width--{{ section.settings.section_width | default: 'wide' }} color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme.id }}"
    style="--section-padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px; --section-padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px; --columns-desktop: {{ columns_desktop }}; --columns-mobile: {{ columns_mobile }};"
    {% if section.settings.show_only_empty_cart %}
      data-cart-refresh
    {% endif %}
  >
    <product-list-ui class="product-list__inner">
      {%- comment -%}
        A hidden h2 for the product titles (h3) when no heading block shows one. The section can't read
        its blocks (Tab blocks count in section.blocks), so it is always written and CSS removes it when
        the heading area has its own h1 / h2.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <h2 class="visually-hidden product-list__fallback-heading">{{ 'products.list_heading' | t }}</h2>

      {%- comment -%}
        One content_for blocks tag only (Shopify allows one per file, even in separate if branches), in a wrapper that depends on the
        layout:
        - Tabs: every block draws itself in one flow: Heading / Text / Button blocks as the heading area,
          each Tab block as its tab button + product panel (blocks/_product-tab). The script moves the tab
          buttons into the empty tab row (role="tablist") and shows one panel. The flow is a grid: the
          heading area on the left with the tab row on the right from 750px, the tab row under the
          heading on phones, the panels under both. Before the script runs, only the first panel shows
          and the tab row keeps its height (no jump). Without JavaScript the tab row is hidden and every
          panel shows with its tab name as a heading.
        - Other layouts: the heading area in the top bar (with the strip's arrows), the products under it.
          Tab blocks draw nothing there.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        # Nested ifs: one logical operator per condition (project rule). A top bar that only holds Tab
        # blocks left over from the Tabs layout (they draw nothing here) is hidden by CSS.
        assign show_top = false
        if layout == 'tabs' or layout == 'strip'
          assign show_top = true
        endif
        if section.blocks.size > 0
          assign show_top = true
        endif
      -%}
      {%- if show_top -%}
        {%- if layout == 'tabs' -%}
          <animate-on-scroll class="product-list__flow">
            <div class="product-list__tablist" role="tablist" aria-label="{{ 'products.tabs_label' | t | escape }}" data-tablist></div>
            {%- if request.design_mode -%}
              {%- comment -%} Theme editor only, hidden by CSS once a Tab shows {%- endcomment -%}
              <p class="product-list__tab-off product-list__editor-note">{{ 'products.tabs_editor_empty' | t }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
        {%- else -%}
          <div class="product-list__top">
            <div class="product-list__header">
        {%- endif -%}

        {% content_for 'blocks' %}

        {%- if layout == 'tabs' -%}
          </animate-on-scroll>
        {%- else -%}
            </div>
            {%- if layout == 'strip' -%}
              <div class="product-list__arrows">
                <button type="button" class="product-list__arrow" data-strip-prev disabled>
                  <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'products.previous' | t }}</span>
                  {{- 'icon-arrow.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
                </button>
                <button type="button" class="product-list__arrow" data-strip-next>
                  <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'products.next' | t }}</span>
                  {{- 'icon-arrow.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
                </button>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- unless layout == 'tabs' -%}
        <animate-on-scroll>
          {% render 'product-list-items',
            collection: product_collection,
            limit: limit,
            layout: layout,
            image_ratio: section.settings.image_ratio,
            show_secondary_image: section.settings.show_secondary_image,
            sizes: card_sizes,
            animation: animation
          %}
        </animate-on-scroll>
      {%- endunless -%}
    </product-list-ui>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .product-list {
    padding-block: var(--section-padding-top) var(--section-padding-bottom);
  }

  /* The "Section width" setting (critical.css: --section-width), minus the page margins */
  .product-list__inner {
    display: block;
    inline-size: min(
      calc(var(--section-width, var(--page-width)) - var(--page-margin) * 2),
      calc(100% - var(--page-margin) * 2)
    );
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  /* Top bar: the heading area on the left, the tabs or the strip's arrows on the right */
  .product-list__top {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-md) var(--space-lg);
    margin-block-end: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  /* Heading area: blocks stack with space between */
  .product-list__header {
    display: flex;
    flex: 1 1 20rem;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .product-list__items {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  /* Grid and tabs: the big cards in columns */
  .product-list__items--grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--columns-mobile), minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md);
  }

  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .product-list__items--grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--columns-desktop), minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: var(--space-xl);
    }
  }

  /* Each card fills its grid cell, so cards in a row are equal height */
  .product-list__items--grid .product-list__item,
  .product-list__items--grid .product-list__item > .product-card {
    block-size: 100%;
  }

  /* Compact rows: one per row on phones, two per row from 750px (empty-bag mockup "Main") */
  .product-list__items--rows {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .product-list__items--rows {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  /* Both cards in a row the same height (a unit price line makes one taller) */
  .product-list__items--rows .product-list__item,
  .product-list__items--rows .product-row-card {
    block-size: 100%;
  }

  /*
    Scrolling strip: one row that scrolls sideways; each card snaps to the left edge. The scrollbar is
    hidden (the arrows and touch swipes move it), padding keeps the cards' shadows from being cut off.
  */
  .product-list__items--strip {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    overflow-x: auto;
    overscroll-behavior-inline: contain;
    padding-block: var(--space-xs) var(--space-md);
    scroll-snap-type: inline mandatory;
    scrollbar-width: none;
  }

  .product-list__items--strip::-webkit-scrollbar {
    display: none;
  }

  .product-list__items--strip .product-list__item {
    flex: none;
    inline-size: clamp(14rem, 22vw, 20rem);
    scroll-snap-align: start;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .product-list__items--strip {
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
    }
  }

  /* Round outline arrows; the left one is the right arrow turned around */
  .product-list__arrows {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .product-list .product-list__arrow {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    inline-size: 2.75rem;
    min-block-size: 0;
    block-size: 2.75rem;
    padding: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-text);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: none;
    box-shadow: none;
    color: var(--color-text);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .product-list .product-list__arrow:hover:not(:disabled) {
    background-color: var(--color-text);
    color: var(--color-background);
  }

  .product-list .product-list__arrow:disabled {
    opacity: 0.35;
    cursor: default;
  }

  .product-list__arrow svg {
    inline-size: 1rem;
    block-size: 1rem;
  }

  .product-list__arrow[data-strip-prev] svg {
    rotate: 180deg;
  }

  /* Right-to-left pages: "next" goes to the left, so both arrows point the other way */
  .product-list__arrows:dir(rtl) svg {
    scale: -1 1;
  }

  /*
    Tabs layout: one grid for the heading blocks, the tab row and the Tab blocks' panels (all drawn in one
    flow, see the markup). Phones: one column (heading, tab row, panels). From 750px: the heading blocks on
    the left, the tab row on the right of the first row (empty-bag mockup "Tabs"), the panels under both.
    <product-tab> (one per Tab block) has no box of its own: its button and panel are grid items.
    No Tab shows (all off, or no products on the store): the section shows nothing.
  */
  .product-list--tabs.product-list--live:not(:has(product-tab)) {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Theme editor: the note "Add a Tab block..." shows only while no Tab shows */
  .product-list__flow:has(product-tab) .product-list__editor-note {
    display: none;
  }

  /* The hidden h2 goes when the heading area has its own h1 / h2 (display: none = not read either) */
  .product-list:has(:is(.product-list__header, .product-list__flow) :is(h1, h2)) .product-list__fallback-heading {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Top bar with nothing in it (only Tab blocks left over from the Tabs layout): no empty gap */
  .product-list__top:not(:has(.product-list__arrows, .product-list__header > :not(.shopify-block), .product-list__header > .shopify-block > *)) {
    display: none;
  }

  .product-list__flow {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: end;
    gap: var(--space-md) var(--space-lg);
  }

  /*
    Shopify puts each theme block in a wrapper (<div class="shopify-block">); without a box of its own,
    the block's content (heading, text, tab button, panel) takes part in this grid. The rules below also
    work when there is no wrapper.
  */
  .product-list__flow > .shopify-block,
  .product-list__tab-item {
    display: contents;
  }

  .product-list__flow > *,
  .product-list__flow > .shopify-block > *,
  .product-list__tab-item > .product-list__panel {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .product-list__tablist {
    order: 1;
    justify-self: start;
  }

  .product-list__tab-item > .product-list__panel {
    order: 2;
    margin-block-start: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .product-list__tab-off {
    order: 2;
    margin: 0;
    font-style: italic;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .product-list__flow {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    }

    /* The heading blocks in the first column (not the tab row, Tab blocks or the editor note) */
    .product-list__flow > :not(.product-list__tablist, .product-list__tab-item, .product-list__tab-off, .shopify-block),
    .product-list__flow > .shopify-block > :not(.product-list__tab-item, .product-list__tab-off) {
      grid-column: 1;
    }

    .product-list__flow > .product-list__tablist {
      grid-column: 2;
      grid-row: 1;
      justify-self: end;
    }
  }

  /* Tabs: a glass pill holding the tab buttons; the chosen tab is the solid button colour */
  .product-list__tablist {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.375rem;
    padding: 0.25rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background-color: var(--color-glass-strong);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow), var(--glass-rim);
  }

  /* With JavaScript, before the script moves the buttons in: the row keeps its height (no jump) */
  .js .product-list__tablist:empty {
    min-block-size: 3rem;
    min-inline-size: 12rem;
  }

  .product-list .product-list__tab {
    min-block-size: 2.5rem;
    padding-block: 0;
    padding-inline: 1.25rem;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: none;
    box-shadow: none;
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: var(--font-size-small);
    letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-nav);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .product-list .product-list__tab[aria-selected='true'] {
    background-color: var(--color-button);
    color: var(--color-button-text);
  }

  /* A button still in its Tab block (no script yet, or none) is hidden; the tab row shows the moved ones */
  .product-list__tab-item > .product-list__tab {
    display: none;
  }

  /*
    With JavaScript only the chosen tab's panel shows. Before the script runs, only the first Tab's panel
    shows: a Tab block that comes after another Tab block hides its panel (with the Shopify block wrapper,
    and without it). Without JavaScript every panel shows with its tab name, and there is no tab row.
  */
  .js product-list-ui:defined .product-list__panel:not(.is-active),
  .js product-list-ui:not(:defined) .shopify-block:has(product-tab) ~ .shopify-block .product-list__panel,
  .js product-list-ui:not(:defined) .product-list__tab-item ~ .product-list__tab-item > .product-list__panel,
  .no-js .product-list__tablist {
    display: none;
  }

  /*
    With JavaScript the tab row shows the tab names, so the panel's h3 title is visually hidden; screen
    readers still get it, so the outline stays h2 section, h3 tab, h4 products (as without JavaScript).
  */
  .js .product-list__panel-title {
    position: absolute;
    inline-size: 1px;
    block-size: 1px;
    margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .product-list__panel-title {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
    font-size: var(--font-size-h3);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% javascript %}
  /**
   * <product-list-ui>: the Product list's two interactive layouts.
   * - Tabs: each Tab block draws its button + panel (blocks/_product-tab); the buttons are moved into the
   *   tab row here. Clicking a tab (or ← / → / Home / End on the tab row) shows its panel. In the theme
   *   editor, selecting a Tab block shows its panel.
   * - Scrolling strip: the arrows scroll by about one screen of cards and turn off at either end (checked
   *   again on scroll and on resize; right-to-left pages too).
   * All listeners on one AbortController: the editor can attach the element again (a moved section).
   */
  class ProductListUI extends HTMLElement {
    connectedCallback() {
      this.controller = new AbortController();
      const { signal } = this.controller;

      // Tabs: each Tab block drew its own button (hidden in the block); move them into the tab row, in
      // block order, and show one panel (the one already chosen after an editor re-attach, else the first)
      this.tablist = this.querySelector('[data-tablist]');
      this.tabs = [...this.querySelectorAll('[data-tab]')];
      if (this.tablist && this.tabs.length) {
        this.tablist.append(...this.tabs);
        // The tab row is named after the heading block (its h2), else it keeps "Product tabs"
        const heading = this.querySelector('.product-list__flow h2')?.textContent.trim();
        if (heading) this.tablist.setAttribute('aria-label', heading);
        this.select(this.tabs.find((tab) => tab.getAttribute('aria-selected') === 'true') || this.tabs[0]);
      }
      this.tabs.forEach((tab) => {
        tab.addEventListener('click', () => this.select(tab), { signal });
        tab.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => this.onTabKey(event, tab), { signal });
      });
      // Theme editor: selecting a Tab block (its panel carries the block's editor attributes) shows it
      if (this.tabs.length && window.Shopify?.designMode) {
        document.addEventListener(
          'shopify:block:select',
          (event) => {
            const tab = this.tabs.find((item) => item.getAttribute('aria-controls') === event.target.id);
            if (tab) this.select(tab);
          },
          { signal }
        );
      }

      this.track = this.querySelector('[data-strip-track]');
      this.prev = this.querySelector('[data-strip-prev]');
      this.next = this.querySelector('[data-strip-next]');
      if (this.track && this.prev && this.next) {
        this.prev.addEventListener('click', () => this.scrollStrip(-1), { signal });
        this.next.addEventListener('click', () => this.scrollStrip(1), { signal });
        this.track.addEventListener('scroll', () => this.updateArrows(), { passive: true, signal });
        // A resize, or pictures that load, change how much there is to scroll
        this.resizeObserver = new ResizeObserver(() => this.updateArrows());
        this.resizeObserver.observe(this.track);
        if (this.track.firstElementChild) this.resizeObserver.observe(this.track.firstElementChild);
        this.updateArrows();
      }
    }

    disconnectedCallback() {
      this.controller?.abort();
      this.resizeObserver?.disconnect();
    }

    select(tab, focus = false) {
      this.tabs.forEach((other) => {
        const selected = other === tab;
        other.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(selected));
        other.tabIndex = selected ? 0 : -1; // one tab stop for the whole tab row
        document.getElementById(other.getAttribute('aria-controls'))?.classList.toggle('is-active', selected);
      });
      if (focus) tab.focus();
    }

    onTabKey(event, tab) {
      const index = this.tabs.indexOf(tab);
      const last = this.tabs.length - 1;
      const rtl = getComputedStyle(this).direction === 'rtl';
      const forward = rtl ? 'ArrowLeft' : 'ArrowRight';
      const back = rtl ? 'ArrowRight' : 'ArrowLeft';
      const moves = { [forward]: index === last ? 0 : index + 1, [back]: index === 0 ? last : index - 1, Home: 0, End: last };
      if (!(event.key in moves)) return;
      event.preventDefault();
      this.select(this.tabs[moves[event.key]], true);
    }

    /** "Next" goes along the reading direction (to the left on right-to-left pages) */
    scrollStrip(step) {
      const rtl = getComputedStyle(this.track).direction === 'rtl';
      this.track.scrollBy({ left: step * (rtl ? -1 : 1) * this.track.clientWidth * 0.8 });
    }

    /** Arrows turn off at either end (1px slack for rounding). scrollLeft is 0 or negative in RTL. */
    updateArrows() {
      const { scrollLeft, scrollWidth, clientWidth } = this.track;
      const position = Math.abs(scrollLeft);
      this.prev.disabled = position <= 1;
      this.next.disabled = position + clientWidth >= scrollWidth - 1;
    }
  }

  if (!customElements.get('product-list-ui')) customElements.define('product-list-ui', ProductListUI);
{% endjavascript %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:general.product_list",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "@theme"
    },
    {
      "type": "_product-tab"
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:labels.content"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "layout",
      "label": "t:labels.product_list_layout",
      "info": "t:labels.product_list_layout_info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "grid",
          "label": "t:options.product_list_layout.grid"
        },
        {
          "value": "rows",
          "label": "t:options.product_list_layout.rows"
        },
        {
          "value": "strip",
          "label": "t:options.product_list_layout.strip"
        },
        {
          "value": "tabs",
          "label": "t:options.product_list_layout.tabs"
        }
      ],
      "default": "grid"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:labels.products"
    },
    {
      "type": "collection",
      "id": "collection",
      "label": "t:labels.collection",
      "info": "t:labels.product_list_collection_info"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "products_to_show",
      "label": "t:labels.products_to_show",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 24,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 8
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_only_empty_cart",
      "label": "t:labels.product_list_only_empty_cart",
      "info": "t:labels.product_list_empty_cart_info",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:labels.layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "section_width",
      "label": "t:labels.section_width",
      "info": "t:labels.section_width_info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "narrow",
          "label": "t:options.section_width.narrow"
        },
        {
          "value": "wide",
          "label": "t:options.section_width.wide"
        },
        {
          "value": "widest",
          "label": "t:options.section_width.widest"
        },
        {
          "value": "full",
          "label": "t:options.section_width.full"
        }
      ],
      "default": "wide"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "columns_desktop",
      "label": "t:labels.columns_desktop",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 5,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 4,
